  "measurementNotes": [
    "The candidate was served only to owned browsers under production headers. The final run loaded unmodified public files, without renderer interception.",
    "Earlier renderer build 20261104T112032Z remained byte-identical inside deployment 20261104T165051Z; the raw baseline harness retained the renderer-build label.",
    "The node factory and generic peer could both recover the same failure. Integration regressions prove stale native ICE used the previous login while refresh was pending; the corrected owner defers that restart and its offer.",
    "Both guests share an isolated controlled carrier. Only the proxy container changes WireGuard/NAT routes; the Mac VPN and firewall are unchanged. Browser non-proxied WebRTC UDP is disabled; the proxy accepts port443 only.",
    "Private counters cover the whole node and cannot identify a client, selected path or failed call. Some per-login refusals remain; no claim that all quota refusals are eliminated is made.",
    "The owner reported updating the managing room tab before the production run. Other participant activity is not controlled, so node-wide differences are not a causal capacity comparison.",
    "Selected-pair telemetry is required during recovery confirmations. Missing selected pairs in steady samples are counted separately, not silently treated as verified endpoints.",
    "Displayed frames follow attached visible video elements. RTP freeze counters include inactive slots and retiring generations; they are not a perceptual playback score.",
    "A reconstructed VPN fixture first used the wrong local carrier port. Its HTTPS probe failed, no product pass was inferred, and the corrected fixture passed an independent encrypted-transfer check before reruns.",
    "Browser allocation-error counts use the final cumulative event arrays, including separate events with indistinguishable millisecond timestamps; repeated copies of arrays in earlier samples are not recounted."
  ],
